        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(review): screenshot proof is available to sandboxed reviewers",
        "body": "Closes #594\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where contributors supplying screenshot-only real-behavior proof would have that evidence treated as unviewable by ClawSweeper's network-disabled review sandbox.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nClawSweeper now hydrates linked PNG, JPEG, WebP, and GIF proof through the existing bounded media download path. Downloaded images are exposed directly for local inspection, while videos retain their existing ffprobe and contact-sheet processing. Local-range reviews continue skipping all host media downloads.\n\n## User Impact\n\nScreenshot-only evidence can now be assessed on its merits instead of being structurally classified as insufficient solely because the reviewer cannot access the network. Existing video proof behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before the fix, the focused regression could not discover or hydrate a PNG proof URL, while the identical MOV URL was recognized.\n- `pnpm run build && node --test test/review-prompt-policy.test.ts`: 31/31 passed. Coverage includes image discovery, image artifact preparation, no video-tool invocation for images, mixed image/video ordering, preserved video-only hook behavior, and existing ffprobe/contact-sheet processing.\n- Real production-helper proof on macOS 26.0.1 with Node 24.16.0: served the repository's tracked PNG over a localhost HTTP server and ran the built media preparation helper with the real curl command. Result: `status=prepared`, `kind=image`, `downloaded=true`, `bytes=1478360`, `metadataCreated=false`, `contactSheetCreated=false`, `manifestArtifacts=1`; the server recorded an HTTP 200 GET.\n- `pnpm run check`: passed, including build, lint, 1,180 unit tests with 0 failures, repair tests, changed and full coverage suites, and formatting.\n- Limitation: no live GitHub-hosted ClawSweeper review decision was run; validation covers the production media hydration boundary, generated manifest, prompt guidance, and full local test suite.\n\nDisclosure: AI was used to understand the codebase and review the fix.\n",
